{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n/// Contents paired with the fingerprint of that same observation.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n```\n\nThis type lives in `habeas_sdk::graph`. For node reads, the SDK constructs it by\npassing the identity and the contents returned by `Graph::node_content` to\n`Fingerprinting::fingerprint`, without another read. For a label-specific edge\nquery, the SDK constructs the snapshot from the returned targets and their\ntarget-set fingerprint, without another query.\n`T` needs no filesystem path or source span.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Snapshot<T>` has `content` and `fingerprint` fields.\n2. A node read builds the snapshot by calling `Fingerprinting::fingerprint` on the identity and the contents returned by `Graph::node_content`, with no extra read.\n3. A label-specific edge query builds the snapshot from the returned targets and their target-set fingerprint, with no extra query.\n4. `T` needs no filesystem path or source span.\n\n**Node reads**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` calls `read_snapshot` and asserts `fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`.\n  - It changes the graph contents and then asserts the exact read log `[1, 1, 1, 2]`. This shows each `read` or `read_snapshot` costs exactly one `node_content` call.\n  - It asserts the recorded dependencies carry the fingerprint of the content actually observed, both \"before\" and \"after\".\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` mutates the graph after `read_snapshot`. It then asserts that `graph.fingerprint(&node, &snapshot.content)` equals `snapshot.fingerprint` and that the value is still \"before\". A second read would break this.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` check that recorded node dependencies match the delivered snapshots and that the read order is exact (`reads == [1,3,2,3,1]`).\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that the fingerprint is computed from the supplied retained content, not a fresh read. It does this with `changed.fingerprint(&references, &retained_references)` and the equivalent call on the source node.\n\n**Edge queries**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents]` asserts the recorded `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` carries `edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[3, 5])`. This is the target-set fingerprint of the returned targets. It also asserts that `reads` is empty, so no content is read.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` makes a second edge lookup on the graph return an error, and asserts exactly one lookup. This shows the snapshot is built from the single query and the SDK does not re-query. The same test asserts the recorded fingerprint equals `edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2])`.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` exercises `outgoing_edges(...).content` on a real domain.\n\n**Residual notes**\n- No test asserts the edge `Snapshot.fingerprint` field directly. The recorded dependency asserts cover it, because the dependency fingerprint comes from the snapshot, so a wrong value would fail.\n- Two clauses have no direct test:\n  - The `Clone` and `Debug` derives and the `habeas_sdk::graph` location are type-level facts that need no behavioral test. The tests use the type through that path.\n  - \"`T` needs no path or span\" is a permission, not a behavior. The tests exercise `Snapshot` with plain string, `u8` and `Vec` contents.\n\nThe implementation (`crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`, `prepare_read` and `prepare_edges`) matches this behavior. I did not rely on it to derive expectations.",
